- [/] Orchestration of people and resources envolved (collaboration and effects/details of transfers):  Several parties in same Transfer (A gives to B, C gives to A and B..). Also observes, that can satiate some transfer they are participating by looking into another transfer without participating (anonymously).

- [/] Resources
	- [/] I can setup an amount of resources flowing out of my Organ and going into another Organ. That means a one way Transfer, functioning more like a donation.
	- [/] I can compose a two way Transfer, functioning like a Trade.
	- [/] I can say how much should go to the other party's resources, how much I am willing to contribute with some Record, and have the amount that is publicly being Contributed by me be different from the one i contabilize internally in my Lince: saying I will pay you 10 might make me internally diminish my 'Money' Record by 5 instead. I still will pay 10, but I control how my resources fluctuate with Transfers internally.
	- [/] Surplus can be projected. (Surplus = quantity you have beyond what is already committed to hard reservations — the "safe to give away" figure. Formula: `record.quantity - reserved_quantity`. Distinct from `available_quantity` in that surplus could also account for confirmed incoming deliveries not yet settled.)

- [/] Agreement
	- [/] Agreement state can also be derived for a parent Transfer.
	- [/] Dependency agreement mode is wired to interaction dependency satisfaction. (Agreement is complete when the depended-on Transfer itself is agreed/settled, not when local parties sign. Requires querying `transfer_interaction` rows with `depends_on` kind and checking the referenced Transfer state.)

- [/] Be able to combine many possible records to be changed in a transfer internally, but only showing it as one record externally. I break my bike, need to go to work tomorrow. Bike and Transport to Work are internal Needs tomorrow, but i can post a Transfer to the world that says 'Bike broke, need to go to work tomorrow'. I can decide if someone gives me a #bike i can satiate it and the need to go to work.
	- [/] If they lend me for 3 days they are both still fullfiled, but i see it in a timeline becoming a need again after a while, i can then post the need now or only when i actually need it.
