Ontology in Lince can be a castle, it is for managing the content of your database. The meaning of records through Lingua Vocabulary, in the tasks it is referred as the central point for guaranteeing you have the data you want, dealing with sync and organ discovery, it is the vibe of several features in Lince. These are the remaining tasks of several features related to this Ontology vibe:

# Organ Profile and Discovery:
- [ ] One of the ways to get data from an organ that is more byte heavy (i believe some discovery formats are limited, maybe you can only get this much data after getting the person's iroh address and wanting to see more) is one where they send their profile picture, header picture, name of organ, and some description. This can be a pattern for now and wire into existing properties of organs, like adding it's public address so you add them, and other organ stuff, not too many.
	- [ ] Would it be cool to be able to post it in a Lince server? So you call that server for the profile instead of asking them directly? They would need to be online if not and would make the anonymous-request/individual-ddos-prevention a hard thing to balance? How could it not? Could an organ be like having a profile/user in some public Lince organ and linking that user to a personal organ in the bio or something? We would be maintaining two identities, but it would be like having a profile in linkedin and a personal website, not the craziest. We could try and mirror both?
